          "raw_bytes": 5889,
          "lf_bytes": 5889,
          "raw_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0",
          "lf_sha256": "867f37d31c89be99b7218d384e7e1eafec857b4f0da5f51191f6f314828f91c0"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          727706,
          733595
        ],
        "literal_source_text": "Relative to the decomposition \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} , we write an operator \\mathsf{T} on \\mathfrak{H} in block form as \\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned} (B.3) The first subscript specifies the target subspace and the second the source subspace; thus \\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\\mathfrak{H}_{b}\\to\\mathfrak{H}_{a} for a,b\\in\\{\\mathsf{P},\\perp\\} ."
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.SS1.p3",
        "coverage": "NODE",
        "reason": "Selfadjoint unitary reflection gives scalar selfadjoint contraction context; printed B5 block conclusions separately EXCLUDED.",
        "qualified_raw_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p3-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 8702,
          "lf_bytes": 8702,
          "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
          "lf_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873"
        },
        "qualified_LF_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-SS1-p3-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 8702,
          "lf_bytes": 8702,
          "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
          "lf_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          733596,
          742298
        ],
        "literal_source_text": "We first apply this block notation to the reflection map \\mathsf{U} from ( 2.14 ). We use the same symbol for its pullback on observables: (\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4) This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix \\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,. Here \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to itself, whereas \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . Since \\mathsf{U} is self-adjoint and unitary, \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} is a self-adjoint contraction on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} . Writing \\mathsf{U}^{2}=I in blocks gives \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.E8",
        "coverage": "NODE",
        "reason": "Yplus/Yminus reflection law context; no rate conclusion.",
        "qualified_raw_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-E8-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 1729,
          "lf_bytes": 1729,
          "raw_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
          "lf_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a"
        },
        "qualified_LF_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-E8-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 1729,
          "lf_bytes": 1729,
          "raw_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
          "lf_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          762524,
          764253
        ],
        "literal_source_text": "Y_{+}\\coloneqq X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\\coloneqq X-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptX\\sim\\mu\\,. (B.8)"
      },
      {
        "id": "A3.SS1.p2",
        "coverage": "NODE",
        "reason": "Reflected every-state normalized density only; score derivative/C1 EXCLUDED.",
        "qualified_raw_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A3-SS1-p2-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 5406,
          "lf_bytes": 5406,
          "raw_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b",
          "lf_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b"
        },
        "qualified_LF_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A3-SS1-p2-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 5406,
          "lf_bytes": 5406,
          "raw_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b",
          "lf_sha256": "96d3f106bcd0b32f60a5c97b7df3d8f231c571d286884e8ca4aa30cf3b64749b"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          1004189,
          1009595
        ],
        "literal_source_text": "Recall that the conditional density p_{y} of Y_{-} given Y_{+}=y is p_{y}(u)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{\\|y-u\\|^{2}}{8\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,, and define s_{y}(u)\\coloneqq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{y-u}{4\\eta}\\,. Differentiating the normalized conditional density gives \\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathrm{Cov}\\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)\\,. (C.1)"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.Thmtheorem1.p1",
        "coverage": "NODE",
        "reason": "Literal beta eta<=1 binder context ONLY; rho/gamma and whole theorem conclusions EXCLUDED.",
        "qualified_raw_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-Thmtheorem1-p1-dffe0a792ef0.raw.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 2966,
          "lf_bytes": 2966,
          "raw_sha256": "3ecbbc427d67888cc1fc83578053d55b218d901d0a231cd9aa29b037f61288ec",
          "lf_sha256": "3ecbbc427d67888cc1fc83578053d55b218d901d0a231cd9aa29b037f61288ec"
        },
        "qualified_LF_slice": {
          "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-defect-root61/next-macro-source62/primary-A2-Thmtheorem1-p1-dffe0a792ef0.LF.snapshot",
          "raw_bytes": 2966,
          "lf_bytes": 2966,
          "raw_sha256": "3ecbbc427d67888cc1fc83578053d55b218d901d0a231cd9aa29b037f61288ec",
          "lf_sha256": "3ecbbc427d67888cc1fc83578053d55b218d901d0a231cd9aa29b037f61288ec"
        },
        "byte_range": [
          774554,
          777520
        ],
        "literal_source_text": "Assume \\beta\\eta\\leq 1 , and set \\rho_{\\rm mac}\\coloneqq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\coloneqq\\sqrt{1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,. (B.12) Note that \\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\geq\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta} . Then the following hold."
      }
    ],
    "source_first_pid": 11948,
